WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.560
Although fans still have to wait almost a
year to see "The Batman" – set to hit theaters

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.090
on March 4th, 2022 — thanks to trailers
and leaks, we’re already getting a sense

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.420
of what the film will look and feel like.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.650
One of the latest leaks features Paul Dano's
Riddler, who gets only a brief appearance

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.689
in the one trailer for "The Batman" that's
been released thus far.

00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:23.010
The new image gives a clearer look at how
Dano's version of the Riddler will be styled

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.849
in the Matt Reeves-directed film.

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:28.890
If the watermark on several versions of the
photo that are currently circulating social

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.610
media is to be believed, it may have come
to us courtesy of Australian-based filmmaker

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.300
and content creator Ryan Unicomb.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.440
The original source of the leaked photo is
unknown at this time, but it seems to be part

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.650
of a poster, calendar, or other piece of promotional
artwork that hasn't been formally released

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:46.650
yet.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.180
In the freshly leaked photo — which we aren't
going to share here given that it's, well,

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.610
leaked and we’re not getting in trouble!

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.430
– Paul Dano's version of the Riddler has
his face completely covered, just like he

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.250
does in the trailer for "The Batman."

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.440
He's shown wearing glasses and a leather face
mask with eye holes, and the image as a whole

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.920
provides a much clearer idea of how he'll
present himself than the super-dark trailer

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.920
did.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.719
The mask appears to have a flap for the Riddler's
mouth that can be covered, and doesn't seem

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:11.719
to be very high-tech.

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:16.530
Instead, it has a distinctly rough feel, as
if Dano's character sewed the whole thing

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.659
together himself.

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:22.350
Basically, he looks like The Machine from
the movie 8 mm — with glasses and a velcro

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:23.609
strip over the mouth.

00:01:23.609 --> 00:01:27.940
It's much different than the way the Riddler
has been depicted in DC comics before.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.909
In the comics, the Riddler has historically
been shown decked out in shades of green,

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:37.240
purple, and black, sporting over-the-top costumes
emblazoned with his trademark question mark

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.250
insignia.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.750
This is the look that Jim Carrey adopted when
he played Edward Nygma, aka the Riddler, in

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.109
Tim Burton's 1995 flick "Batman Forever."

00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:50.840
A Riddler wearing a full mask that looks totally
homemade is a far cry from what fans are used

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.840
to seeing.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.270
After getting a glimpse of the leaked image,
fans have expressed their excitement for the

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:58.929
approach that director Matt Reeves appears
to be taking with "The Batman."

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:00.139
One fan wrote on Twitter,

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:04.409
"The Zodiac Killer vibes Riddler is giving
off in Matt Reeves' 'The Batman' is the exact

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:06.789
reason why I know he's going to blow our minds."

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:07.829
Another user added,

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:11.280
"I have no issue with the Riddler's new look
in 'The Batman' 2022.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.830
He looks frightening and iconic in his own
unique way.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:18.140
It's an intriguing reinterpretation of this
character.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:22.320
We've had plenty of classic Riddler looks
on screen now so I'm fully embracing this

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.320
fresh take."

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.880
"The Batman" is set in the early days of Bruce
Wayne's time as a crime-fighter and protector

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:32.620
of Gotham, and Dano's Riddler is set to be
the film's main villain, a serial killer who

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.370
begins leaving clues behind at the scene of
his murders.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.480
The element of clues makes the Zodiac Killer
a fairly natural point of comparison for Dano's

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.480
version of the Riddler.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.340
For those unaware, the Zodiac Killer was a
serial killer who murdered seemingly random

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.590
people in northern California in the '60s
and — according to the murderer himself

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.730
— '70s.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:55.650
He famously taunted the police and newspapermen
with letters and ciphers — one of which

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.040
was only deciphered in 2020.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.250
It seems Dano's Riddler will do something
similar; in the trailer, Batman reads a cryptic

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.690
letter the Riddler left behind on a dead body.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.720
All a part of his love of riddles, right?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.660
For countless fans, this newly leaked photo
of the Riddler's mask only reaffirms beliefs

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:13.410
that Dano’s Riddler will be one for the
ages.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.720
One user wrote on Twitter,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.730
"Even though we have to wait until next year,
I just can't help but have the feeling that

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:21.860
Paul Dano is going to crush it as The Riddler
in 'The Batman.'

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.180
This could be potentially one of the best
comic book movie villains."

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.690
Another Twitter user tweeted,

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:30.930
"Paul Dano's Riddler is going to be one of
the greatest [comic book movie] villain performances

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.120
of all time mark my words."

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.270
Back in May 2020, Dano spoke to the Playlist,
revealing that he was excited about what "The

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.270
Batman" could be.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:42.980
Joking that he couldn't say much about the
film without getting in trouble, Dano said,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.460
"I feel really good about it.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.240
I think Matt Reeves is the real deal.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.900
I was really surprised by his script, which
I think is, is potentially really powerful.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.650
[...] There's something fun there in my character
and in all the characters.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:58.180
It's the kind of movie that we're just desperate
to share on the big screen in a big way.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.310
... It will be worth [the wait].

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.240
It's going to be really cool."

